1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,186
Sound familiar? Three Linux
machines, three updates.

2
00:00:04,286 --> 00:00:08,660
And each one downloads the same
packages from the internet again.

3
00:00:09,311 --> 00:00:11,194
Cache & Carry solves this.

4
00:00:11,294 --> 00:00:14,674
The first machine downloads
a package from the internet.

5
00:00:14,774 --> 00:00:17,236
All others get it straight
from your network.

6
00:00:17,886 --> 00:00:20,154
Live traffic shows it exactly.

7
00:00:20,254 --> 00:00:23,674
On the first request the
package comes from the internet.

8
00:00:23,774 --> 00:00:26,309
For the next machine it
comes from the cache.

9
00:00:26,959 --> 00:00:31,732
Cache & Carry is a lean, self-hosted
package cache for your network.

10
00:00:31,832 --> 00:00:36,951
For APT and Pacman, with a dashboard,
statistics and storage limits.

11
00:00:37,051 --> 00:00:38,749
Free and open source.

12
00:00:39,399 --> 00:00:43,316
You can install it in three
ways. All with the same version.

13
00:00:44,399 --> 00:00:46,299
One: Proxmox VE.

14
00:00:46,399 --> 00:00:55,140
One command on the host creates an unprivileged Debian container,
verifies the checksum and installs the latest release.

15
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:58,607
At the end you see the
address and the setup token.

16
00:00:58,707 --> 00:01:03,019
An update is the same command with
update and the container number.

17
00:01:03,669 --> 00:01:04,922
Two: Docker.

18
00:01:05,022 --> 00:01:14,417
The image is available for amd64 and arm64. It is
smaller than 16 megabytes and contains no shell.

19
00:01:14,517 --> 00:01:16,858
A single Docker command is enough.

20
00:01:17,508 --> 00:01:19,513
Three: Debian or Ubuntu.

21
00:01:19,613 --> 00:01:24,506
Download the package from the release,
unpack it and run the install script.

22
00:01:24,606 --> 00:01:32,067
Cache & Carry then runs as a systemd
service, also in a VM or on a Raspberry Pi.

23
00:01:32,167 --> 00:01:35,358
To update, run the script
again with the new version.

24
00:01:36,008 --> 00:01:39,277
Then open the web interface on port 8080.

25
00:01:39,377 --> 00:01:42,021
Enter the token, choose a password, done.

26
00:01:44,008 --> 00:01:47,778
You will find all commands on
the website and on GitHub.

27
00:01:47,878 --> 00:01:51,983
Cache & Carry is open source.
Feel free to leave a star.

28
00:01:52,083 --> 00:01:58,504
If this video helps you: subscribe to the channel,
leave a like and tell me in the comments how you use it.
